News - Guizhou's "Eleventh Five-Year Plan" invested 5 billion to solve the problem of drinking water for 10.6 million rural population
Guizhou's "Eleventh Five-Year Plan" invested 5 billion to solve the problem of drinking water for 10.6 million rural population News
In the construction site of the “Anda New Long-distance Pipeline Water Conveyance Project” in Jinsha County, various types of construction machinery are busy at the water source site and pipeline laying site to ensure that the main project is basically completed by the end of the year.
Comrades from the People ’s Drinking Department of the Water Resources Department said that there are more than 100 people ’s drinking projects under construction like this.
From 1996 to 2004, Guizhou Province implemented two phases of the “Desire Project” and “Poverty Relief Project”, which helped more than 18 million rural people in Guizhou Province “thirst out”, but the survey and evaluation in 2005 showed that 23 million rural people in Guizhou Province The population suffers from unsafe drinking water.
It is expected that by the end of this year, the province will invest a total of 4.944 billion yuan in rural drinking water projects. Among them, the central government invested 3.012 billion yuan, and the provincial-level fiscal arrangements for 1.546 billion yuan benefited the farmers’ cumulative investment and labor-discounted capital of more than 300 million yuan.
