From making better use of public transport, to walking or cycling, to using lower consumption equipment, and much more. In addition, you should know that there are many open-source projects that can help against climate change.
Electricitymap Contrib: you can see in real time the CO2 emissions associated with electricity consumption.
Sustainable open technology: a list of open and sustainable technology projects to preserve the stable climate.
GlobalWarning: a project for Minecraft lovers who want to learn about climate change.
Climate Strike License- Software license to prevent some oil and gas companies from continuing to increase fossil fuel extraction.
Shit smoke: an app for iOS and Android mobile devices to see the air pollution of your city measured in equivalent cigarettes.
Climate change data: a list of APIs, open data and ML / AI projects on climate change.
Sustainability- A list of all the sustainable things you should know about.
Liquid Prep: a comprehensive solution for farmers seeking to optimize the use of water in irrigation, especially in times of drought.
Vegginner: app to improve consumption habits and fight against climate change, and even fight against hunger in the world.
