La SARS-CoV-2 pandemic it has altered the way in which daily activities are carried out, such as work. Due to the risk of contagion, teleworking has increased since the State of Alarm was declared and, with the new outbreaks, it will continue to be an alternative so as not to completely paralyze the activity of a company.
Asterisk and how it can help communications in times of pandemic
With Asterisk you will have a IP switchboard It can be used by freelancers who need communication for their activity, and also companies of all sizes. In fact, it is a system that is already used by many companies such as IBM, Google, and many others.
An IP telephone exchange or IP PBX It basically consists of one or more SIP phones (clients), and a server. With them, it is possible to make an internal call through a directory of telephones / users present in the internal network, or to route an external call through VoIP.
Important savings when using VoIP providers, especially when making long distance or international calls.
Scalable, to be able to add more clients when it is needed.
Therefore, you should start adapt your business with the necessary technology, if you haven't already. The virus cannot paralyze the entire country again, since that would entail other associated problems almost as dramatic as the pandemic itself.
Good hygiene and disinfection of hands, utensils, surfaces and areas of common use. With effective products such as hydroalcoholic gels, it gives at least 70%, as well as cleaning products such as bleach.
Promote teleworking compared to the face-to-face model and / or give your clients the possibility to operate digitally. To do this, you should arm yourself with some interesting technologies that can help you, such as Asterisk.
Because the «telephone exchange» is a medium or large building that contained all the terminals of the switched network and the DSLAMs. Now, I suppose that will have changed but it is so.
One of the main advantages is being able to telework connected to the company's VPN and answering the company's phone as if you were in the office.
