During the month of May, the final version of Fedora 26 was scheduled to be released. This would be the product of a series of development versions that would begin to be public during the month of March.
But today it will not be possible to get the new alpha version of Fedora 26 it will happen next week. The beta version of Fedora 26 is also delayed as well as the rest of the developments, such a launch will occur on May 2, being June 27 when the new version of the free RedHat Linux distribution is officially launched, according to the new calendar.
