ED2K is a file exchange protocol (P2P) (Point-to-Point) in which a server acts as an intermediary to connect clients.
Once successfully connected to a server, we can use the search tool, either locally (the connected server) or globally (all servers), any file and we will get the results that match the search as a response.
Customers don't need to have the entire file to start sharing it. There is a shift system and, when the requesting client reaches the top position, the remote client sends him the part of the file that is available to him.
Even with programs like Popcorn-Time you don't even have to wait for the download to finish. Browsers like Brave even already have a client built in for this protocol.
