Many brides decide to have the father-daughter dance directly after their first dance with their new spouse. But if you don’t want to have the dance after that moment, there are other good times to squeeze it in like after the toasts and before cutting the cake.
While some brides choose a heartfelt, loving song, other brides opt for a song that’s more upbeat and brings a little laughter to the guests. Ultimately it’s up to you.
If you want to dance to a faster, upbeat song, choreographing a routine could be a fun and unexpected idea. But if you’d rather stay with a slower, traditional dance, it might not be necessary.
Tradition is one thing, but this dance is ultimately up to you!
