TPU is a kind of polymer material which is polymerized by diphenylmethane diisocyanate (MDI) or toluene diisocyanate (TDI), macromolecular polyol and low molecular polyol (chain extender). Its molecular structure is composed of rigid blocks obtained by reaction of diphenylmethane diisocyanate (MDI) or toluene diisocyanate (TDI) with chain extender, and flexible blocks obtained by reaction of diphenylmethane diisocyanate (MDI) or toluene diisocyanate (TDI) with macromolecular polyols.
According to the molecular structure, TPU can be divided into polyester type (good oil resistance) and polyether type (good water resistance and oil resistance). The relative density is 1.10-1.25, the polyether type is smaller than the polyester type; according to the processing method, it can be divided into injection molding grade, extrusion grade, blow molding grade, etc.
